<title>UK: Bangladesh tenders for 25,000 T white sugar -trade.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh tenders for 25,000 T white sugar -trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh is to tender to buy 25,000 tonnes of white sugar in two equal shipments, trade sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender is to be held on April 19, with half the required amount to be shipped for June 30 and half for July 15, they said.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Bangladesh bought 25,000 tonnes of white sugar at $346.90 per tonne c &amp; f for shipment by June 9, again split into two equal shipments.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
